# `&` composed functions applied (decision D6 amp-compose; the composition itself: test_amp_compose.pairs.warp)

# the value after the last function goes to the first
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; inc & dbl 3' 8
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; inc & dbl(3)' 8
is! 'square(x) := x * x; twice(x) := 2 * x; square & twice 3' 18
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; [1, 2].map(inc & dbl)' [4 6]
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; (inc & inc & inc)(0)' 3

# between truth values `&` stays `and`
is! 'yes & no' no
is! 'x = 1; x > 0 & x < 3' yes
